#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151890 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3abe724a-6aec-5c11-8a00-d92e616a06d7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Cauchy-Euler Equation with a Repeated Root"}] :question/id #uuid "10aa6257-c3f8-59c6-802e-b4a29fca49ab" :question/math-academy-id "e-6627" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n2x^2 y'' + 6 xy' + 2y = 0, \\qquad x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume the solutions take the form $y=x^\\lambda.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\ny' = \\lambda x^{\\lambda -1}, \\qquad y'' = \\lambda(\\lambda-1)x^{\\lambda-2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+6x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+2{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 2\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+6\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+2{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+6\\lambda +2] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+6\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ 2({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ 2(\\lambda +1)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation has a double root $\\lambda = -1.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={c}_{1}{x}^{-1}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{1}}{x}+\\frac{{c}_{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151891 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f9ca4b7-157d-56c9-9302-e7ad08c615c0" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Involving a Cauchy-Euler Equation with a Repeated Root"}] :question/id #uuid "ff0b0603-e0bf-526a-9b4b-d2a4886ba2c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-6628" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\nx^2 y'' - 19 xy' + 100y = 0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny =c_1 x^{10}+ c_2x ^{10}\\ln x ,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\nx^2 y'' - 19 xy' + 100y = 0, \\quad y(1) = 0,\\quad  y'(1)=1, \\quad x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $c_1$ and $c_2$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- First, we apply the condition $y(1)=0.$ Substituting $y(1)= 0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n0= c_1.\n$$\n\n- Then, we apply the condition $y'(1) = 1.$ Differentiating $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =10{c}_{1}{x}^{9}+{c}_{2}{x}^{9}+10{c}_{2}{x}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y'(1)=1$ and $c_1 = 0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =10{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 1 & =0+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x) = x ^{10}\\ln x .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365032 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f9ca4b7-157d-56c9-9302-e7ad08c615c0" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Involving a Cauchy-Euler Equation with a Repeated Root"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf6a3852-a792-572a-9f76-dfbb805667b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=\\frac{1-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365034} {:answer/id #uuid "8d05a629-0401-55b8-8fc3-c04950d14011" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=\\frac{2-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365035} {:answer/id #uuid "6d91a8f2-6618-569d-855b-133a5f41bdb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=\\frac{2-12\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365036} {:answer/id #uuid "7e24aa64-d378-5ae4-a173-49c886ce0bb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=\\frac{1+8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365037} {:answer/id #uuid "d3454bc9-5774-5f40-93e8-0598caaa8741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=\\frac{1+6\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e24aa64-d378-5ae4-a173-49c886ce0bb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=\\frac{1+8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365037} :answer-field/id #uuid "19436038-d03d-51f0-bd68-15bd652f765a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2f1e33b-97ff-5879-aa46-ccc76aa7159d" :question/math-academy-id "q-102365" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+15x{y}^{′}+49y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={c}_{1}{x}^{-7}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+15x{y}^{′}+49y=0,\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=1,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- First, we apply the condition $y(1)=1.$ Substituting $y(1)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n1={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- Then, we apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=1.$ Differentiating $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-7{c}_{1}{x}^{-8}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-8}-7{c}_{2}{x}^{-8}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ and ${c}_{1}=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-7(1)+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={x}^{-7}+8{x}^{-7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1+8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152529 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3abe724a-6aec-5c11-8a00-d92e616a06d7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Cauchy-Euler Equation with a Repeated Root"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "834070a6-752a-509b-b1ff-2bac02438364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x) = c_{1}x^{-1} + c_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150085} {:answer/id #uuid "85319001-94fc-5a32-ace4-8f6ca3b00959" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x) = c_{1}x + c_{2}x^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150086} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff66833-17bc-51c9-861a-bbbdadc44dae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x) = c_{1}x^{-2} + c_{2}x^{-2}\\ln x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150087} {:answer/id #uuid "18576fab-5f8e-5553-be21-cb8d2d87f47f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x) = c_{1}x + c_{2}x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150088} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0d7089-bf13-5625-a91f-594f02fa590c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x) = c_{1}x + c_{2}x\\ln x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a0d7089-bf13-5625-a91f-594f02fa590c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x) = c_{1}x + c_{2}x\\ln x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150089} :answer-field/id #uuid "95c6adf7-2e86-5655-be09-655a5ccf51ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc350f02-9855-549a-a75a-59038b31fab4" :question/math-academy-id "q-64777" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}-x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }-\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-\\lambda +1] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-\\lambda +1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =1.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{1}+{c}_{2}{x}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365039 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3abe724a-6aec-5c11-8a00-d92e616a06d7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Cauchy-Euler Equation with a Repeated Root"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7991adfd-124b-5978-a79e-43790f8287f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}+{c}_{2}{x}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365041} {:answer/id #uuid "da89c0fa-d06d-5d51-b600-a15e2135523b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-9}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365042} {:answer/id #uuid "78ec5dbf-c09c-52d5-96b8-081cc129b46b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{9}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365043} {:answer/id #uuid "10f4ef86-c373-540f-9cf1-b509789c0307" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-3}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365044} {:answer/id #uuid "7c70529b-554b-55a7-90db-39aa61291536" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{3}+{c}_{2}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da89c0fa-d06d-5d51-b600-a15e2135523b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-9}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365042} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb5e1336-c4e7-5b73-adad-1efcaa3a1e12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365040}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bfe4091b-9228-5687-a530-856a009ea468" :question/math-academy-id "q-64785" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+19x{y}^{′}+81y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+19x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+81{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+19\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+81{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+19\\lambda +81] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+19\\lambda +81 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+18\\lambda +81 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +9)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =-9.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-9}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365046 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3abe724a-6aec-5c11-8a00-d92e616a06d7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Cauchy-Euler Equation with a Repeated Root"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ae9e3ad-3b91-5ae3-bdae-52c0f259c06f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-1}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365048} {:answer/id #uuid "7b415066-80fb-5d6e-bd2f-e5ab2cee989c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365049} {:answer/id #uuid "a42cbb48-3734-5e9d-a87b-e0729fc5c2b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365050} {:answer/id #uuid "d102e145-b174-586c-bb72-1ca00f4ba8d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}t+{c}_{2}t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365051} {:answer/id #uuid "5a912bae-9cdb-5869-a331-da53947f9b5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}t+{c}_{2}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b415066-80fb-5d6e-bd2f-e5ab2cee989c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365049} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1c3b756-b8fa-598b-b22d-2751047099c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "437b3f00-7c42-52b5-95e9-666d55baf0bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-64872" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n2{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+10t{y}^{′}+8y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+10t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+8{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 2\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+10\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+8{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+10\\lambda +8] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+10\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ 2({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =-2.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365053 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3abe724a-6aec-5c11-8a00-d92e616a06d7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Cauchy-Euler Equation with a Repeated Root"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88b4083f-9505-59c0-8bdc-4284e9c10442" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365055} {:answer/id #uuid "343d2827-16a0-588c-a402-74fa1a01f317" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{3}+{c}_{2}{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365056} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a2241d-485a-5141-a8f6-57c37c72db57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365057} {:answer/id #uuid "24d2b9e5-8eb1-5302-a26c-5d801599123e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}t+{c}_{2}{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365058} {:answer/id #uuid "ccf21f8c-2297-51e1-9112-8a84220b47d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1a2241d-485a-5141-a8f6-57c37c72db57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365057} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d4752dd-fe6e-54a9-944c-64c8b47519a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1512dbf9-cc16-58e0-aa9b-511e595bd069" :question/math-academy-id "q-64874" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n2{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+22t{y}^{′}+50y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+22t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+50{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 2\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+22\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+50{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+22\\lambda +50] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+22\\lambda +50 & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}+20\\lambda +50 & =0 \\\\ 2({\\lambda }^{2}+10\\lambda +25) & =0 \\\\ 2(\\lambda +5)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =-5.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365060 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3abe724a-6aec-5c11-8a00-d92e616a06d7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Cauchy-Euler Equation with a Repeated Root"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "258f4e11-f905-5b62-918b-ad08cbb7fed3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-6}+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365062} {:answer/id #uuid "9d69675e-bcb0-505a-9812-a30e1cc13c47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{3}+{c}_{2}{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365063} {:answer/id #uuid "3fec114b-62c2-510c-85a6-8eabda1066f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-6}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365064} {:answer/id #uuid "95145abd-e539-5675-9975-7b1ff81d0e3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{3}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365065} {:answer/id #uuid "e44908d8-7632-5a6b-835d-4172610e573d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{6}+{c}_{2}{t}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fec114b-62c2-510c-85a6-8eabda1066f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-6}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365064} :answer-field/id #uuid "38e1c982-babe-526e-bb48-4165a7e3f0c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d15e1269-9485-5413-b829-3a7378223147" :question/math-academy-id "q-64877" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+13t{y}^{′}+36y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+13t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+36{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+13\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+36{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+13\\lambda +36] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+13\\lambda +36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+12\\lambda +36 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +6)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =-6.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-6}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365067 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f9ca4b7-157d-56c9-9302-e7ad08c615c0" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Involving a Cauchy-Euler Equation with a Repeated Root"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e6afc4e-606f-50cc-8525-cbba16bff4e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=2{x}^{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365069} {:answer/id #uuid "34875ed7-7830-58b6-b68d-87e8c41bdb38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={x}^{-5}(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365070} {:answer/id #uuid "bbed33bd-c0ad-543b-b208-ce2da3cdf389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)={x}^{-5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365071} {:answer/id #uuid "94960d67-13fb-53a7-b8fc-17ff6fa29475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=2{x}^{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365072} {:answer/id #uuid "6c8bafaf-a69c-50f2-9035-04bf5e35d20c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=2{x}^{5}(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c8bafaf-a69c-50f2-9035-04bf5e35d20c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=2{x}^{5}(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365073} :answer-field/id #uuid "25fe885d-855d-5c91-ab1e-5356675f4dfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365068}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5be694f6-babf-5a30-89e1-81d884ac107b" :question/math-academy-id "q-64883" :question/problem "Find the solution of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-9x{y}^{′}+25y=0,\\,y(1)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=4,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}-9x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+25{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }-9\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+25{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-9\\lambda +25] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-9\\lambda +25 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +25 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =5.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{5}+{c}_{2}{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$\n\nSubstituting $y(1)=-2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n-2={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=4.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =5{x}^{4}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}{x}^{4}+5{c}_{2}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=4$ and ${c}_{1}=-2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =5{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 4 & =-10+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =-2{x}^{5}+14{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =2{x}^{5}(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365074 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f9ca4b7-157d-56c9-9302-e7ad08c615c0" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Involving a Cauchy-Euler Equation with a Repeated Root"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41e04819-c84a-5612-a593-8953cdd33b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=\\frac{x}{2}-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365076} {:answer/id #uuid "09e3a1dd-b496-5205-9bf1-1c30247f1631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=x-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365077} {:answer/id #uuid "28f38cd0-d0b9-5705-8418-a2a0c21a778e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=x-4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365078} {:answer/id #uuid "c3122cb3-a808-50ab-947f-03cda206bc14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=x+3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365079} {:answer/id #uuid "a21e2e5e-96b1-5b90-a5ed-51d54ba1bc7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=2x-5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3122cb3-a808-50ab-947f-03cda206bc14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=x+3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365079} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2d9ef70-72e5-5313-9957-9d5f121a4236" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf5f77ff-83c3-538e-955a-4f394527d982" :question/math-academy-id "q-93910" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=0,\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=4,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- First, we apply the condition $y(1)=1.$ Substituting $y(1)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n1={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- Then, we apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=1.$ Differentiating $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ and ${c}_{1}=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =1+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x)=x+3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365081 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f9ca4b7-157d-56c9-9302-e7ad08c615c0" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Involving a Cauchy-Euler Equation with a Repeated Root"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bab014a1-e1ce-5e73-8d6d-fb4d9bed6db9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=2{x}^{4}-{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365083} {:answer/id #uuid "41c64f8d-f5fc-549d-9778-d8035fa055f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=2{x}^{4}-3{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365084} {:answer/id #uuid "463d7dc3-a519-5795-84bf-9fc85f8e98d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=2{x}^{4}-2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365085} {:answer/id #uuid "e971d41e-0455-50cb-9ba1-d20188ad8617" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=-3{x}^{4}-4{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365086} {:answer/id #uuid "7d479d69-1f5b-553c-b668-ef3700376216" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=-2{x}^{4}+3{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "463d7dc3-a519-5795-84bf-9fc85f8e98d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x)=2{x}^{4}-2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365085} :answer-field/id #uuid "1821bf03-8696-5936-b43d-89ababb52a07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1be3b6b0-b399-521e-9afa-ba8e015a4069" :question/math-academy-id "q-93912" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-7x{y}^{′}+16y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={c}_{1}{x}^{4}+{c}_{2}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-7x{y}^{′}+16y=0,\\,y(1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=6,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- First, we apply the condition $y(1)=2.$ Substituting $y(1)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n2={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- Then, we apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=6.$ Differentiating $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =4{c}_{1}{x}^{3}+{c}_{2}{x}^{3}+4{c}_{2}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=6$ and ${c}_{1}=2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =4(2)+{c}_{2} \\\\ 6 & =8+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x)=2{x}^{4}-2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365088 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f9ca4b7-157d-56c9-9302-e7ad08c615c0" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Involving a Cauchy-Euler Equation with a Repeated Root"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4715bb4-d3d7-5695-96ec-bbfb556c0e90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)=2{t}^{9}+3{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365090} {:answer/id #uuid "43cc94c4-9a4b-5aa4-8644-4f2895fc984f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)=4{t}^{9}-3{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365091} {:answer/id #uuid "ec2516f4-c999-5fb4-ab1b-15551e237917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)=3{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365092} {:answer/id #uuid "04f2464e-bb35-5ba4-8f52-7fbf6a8f412e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365093} {:answer/id #uuid "74a6f28f-406f-5236-abcd-5e8917a7eb09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)=-2{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec2516f4-c999-5fb4-ab1b-15551e237917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)=3{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365092} :answer-field/id #uuid "5824c42f-9efc-552b-9a75-6f2151a166c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3fbb58a2-add7-53ba-9d6f-0aac95627952" :question/math-academy-id "q-93915" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}-17t{y}^{′}+81y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={c}_{1}{t}^{9}+{c}_{2}{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}-17t{y}^{′}+81y,\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=3,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- First, we apply the condition $y(1)=0.$ Substituting $y(1)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n0={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- Then, we apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=3.$ Differentiating $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =9{c}_{1}{t}^{8}+{c}_{2}{t}^{8}+9{c}_{2}{t}^{8}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=3$ and ${c}_{1}=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =9{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 3 & =0+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =3{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
